  "phase": "main",
  "description": "观澜 · 选股单股研判预案 — ONE sealed code-agnostic lane, instantiated once per candidate code: text.news + text.research_report (news_digest, DEGRADE) + quant.factor -> quant.backtest (factor_ic, BLOCK) + pv.price_action gather the evidence, text.sentiment feeds a one-round dec.bull <-> dec.bear debate (turn order bull, bear; the bear answers the bull's BullCase through opponent_case) whose judge is the single terminal dec.research_mgr (ResearchPlan@1). text.sentiment is structural, not decoration: dec.research_mgr REQUIRES sentiment and it is its only producer. The evidence and debate nodes are auxiliary because no input on the research_mgr chain accepts ResearchReportExtract/BacktestEvidenceReport/PriceActionFeatureReport/BullCase/BearCase, and a reducer's DebateTranscript is invisible to Phase 1's dependency schema check (which compares the upstream WORKER'S output schema) — the debate binds to its judge through DebateCfg.judge_node_id and its turns are folded into the shared transcript slot by debate.transcript_reducer; wiring the folded transcript into the judge's model request is Phase-9 data-method work, exactly as the reviewed Phase-8 e2e states for itself. The graph is code-agnostic and byte-frozen: no node carries params, so one record digest serves every candidate and ONE ApprovalLease binds the whole batch — the subject enters as a committed RunSubject@1 artifact, run-scoped beside each lane's plan.",
